{"title":"Bioinformatics Data Curator Roadmap","role":"Bioinformatics Data Curator","summary":"A Bioinformatics Data Curator manages, validates, annotates, standardises and maintains biological datasets and database records. The role sits at the intersection of molecular biology, genomics, scientific databases, data quality, metadata and computational tools.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. — Bioinformatics"},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc."}],[{"text":"Course"},{"text":"Bioinformatics"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Data Curator"}],[{"text":"Primary domains"},{"text":"Biological databases, genomics, annotation and data quality"}],[{"text":"Core biology"},{"text":"Molecular biology, genetics, genomics, proteomics"}],[{"text":"Core computing"},{"text":"Python, SQL, Linux, databases"}],[{"text":"Data skills"},{"text":"Metadata, ontology, annotation, validation, standardisation"}],[{"text":"Typical entry"},{"text":"Bioinformatics Data Curator / Scientific Data Associate / Data Annotation Associate"}],[{"text":"Long-term roles"},{"text":"Senior Data Curator → Database Specialist → Bioinformatics Scientist / Data Manager"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Bioinformatics Data Curator, Scientific Data Associate, Biological Data Analyst"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Genomics, protein databases, clinical data, ontology, metadata or scientific knowledge management"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Curator, Bioinformatics Database Specialist, Scientific Data Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"AI-assisted curation, knowledge graphs, automated annotation, FAIR data and biomedical data governance"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for a B.Sc. Bioinformatics graduate, particularly when the student develops strong skills in biology + databases + scripting + scientific annotation."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are career-planning horizons rather than guaranteed promotion timelines."}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Cell biology, genetics and basic programming"},{"text":"University + NPTEL"},{"text":"Python mini-project"},{"text":"Biology + coding foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Molecular biology + Python data handling"},{"text":"University + Biopython"},{"text":"Sequence-analysis notebook"},{"text":"Computational biology"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Biological databases + SQL"},{"text":"NCBI/UniProt resources"},{"text":"Database query project"},{"text":"Data-management capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Sequence annotation + metadata"},{"text":"Public biological databases"},{"text":"Curated sequence records"},{"text":"Curation capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Ontologies, controlled vocabularies and data standards"},{"text":"OBO/NCBI/UniProt resources"},{"text":"Ontology mapping project"},{"text":"Scientific data quality"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Automation + internship"},{"text":"Python/Linux/Git + industry"},{"text":"Curation pipeline"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Genomics/proteomics specialisation"},{"text":"Research project"},{"text":"End-to-end curation project"},{"text":"Professional depth"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Portfolio + placement/PG preparation"},{"text":"Industry + research"},{"text":"GitHub portfolio + case studies"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful starting points include NCBI, UniProt and European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI).","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Technical Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Molecular Biology"},{"type":"p","text":"A curator must understand the scientific meaning of the records being curated."},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DNA"},{"text":"RNA"},{"text":"Proteins"},{"text":"Genes"},{"text":"Genomes"},{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Mutations"},{"text":"Gene expression"},{"text":"Regulatory elements"},{"text":"Genetic variation"},{"text":"Molecular pathways"},{"text":"Evolution"}]}]},{"heading":"Biological Databases","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable navigating and interpreting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NCBI"},{"text":"GenBank"},{"text":"RefSeq"},{"text":"Gene"},{"text":"SRA"},{"text":"GEO"},{"text":"dbSNP"},{"text":"ClinVar"},{"text":"UniProt"},{"text":"PDB"},{"text":"Ensembl"},{"text":"InterPro"},{"text":"Pfam"},{"text":"EMBL-EBI resources"},{"text":"PubMed"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Record","identifier","sequence","annotation","evidence","metadata","cross-reference"]}]},{"heading":"Data Curation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Data normalisation"},{"text":"Data standardisation"},{"text":"Metadata creation"},{"text":"Record reconciliation"},{"text":"Duplicate detection"},{"text":"Error detection"},{"text":"Evidence evaluation"},{"text":"Version control"},{"text":"Provenance"},{"text":"Cross-referencing"},{"text":"Controlled vocabularies"},{"text":"Ontology mapping"},{"text":"Manual annotation"},{"text":"Semi-automated annotation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A good curator should always be able to answer:"},{"type":"p","text":"Where did this information come from, what evidence supports it, and how can another researcher reproduce or verify the decision?"}]},{"